  "finalText": "I've triaged all 14 tickets that were in the new queue, using the handbook rules. Triage time was Mon 2026-03-23 08:10Z, by the service desk clock. I paged no one and opened no incidents, because none of these outages is company-wide.\n\n**Closed (2 tickets that weren't service requests)**\n- T-2010: marketing spam.\n- T-2014: automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Merged duplicates (2 pairs)**\nIn each pair the survivor is the earliest report. Neither pair had a deadline yet, so each survivor got the sev2 deadline of triage time plus 4 hours: 12:10Z today.\n- T-2005 merged into T-2004 (CRM search errors). T-2004 keeps the broader department impact.\n- T-2012 merged into T-2003 (Payments builds failing). T-2003 keeps the broader department impact.\n\n**Severity, deadline and assignee for the 10 remaining tickets**\nSev2 deadlines count straight through on the clock. Sev3 and sev4 deadlines count only business hours, starting when the desk opens at 09:00 today and skipping the 25 March company holiday.\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Deadline (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2001 VPN Berlin (team) | sev3 | Mon 23 Mar 17:00 | E-303 (cover) |\n| T-2013 VPN Lisbon (department) | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-303 (cover) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update (single user) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-302 |\n| T-2004 CRM search (department) | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2002 CRM saved filter (single user) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-203 (cover) |\n| T-2011 Payroll overtime (team) | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2006 Payroll tax code (single user) | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2003 Build pipeline, Payments (department) | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-101 |\n| T-2009 Build pipeline, slow logs (single user) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-102 |\n| T-2007 Phishing / password entered | sev2 | Mon 23 Mar 12:10 | E-601 |\n\n**Where the matrix and rota alone didn't decide it**\n- **T-2006:** the matrix says sev3, but a knowledge-base article (KB-55) makes single-user payroll tickets sev2 during the March payroll close (20–31 March). I left a comment on the ticket explaining this.\n- **T-2007:** it came in as a VPN ticket, but the user typed their password into a fake login page. The handbook treats that as a security incident, so it is sev2 and owned by the security-oncall rotation, not the VPN team. I commented this on the ticket.\n- **Cover for engineers on leave:**\n  - E-301 is on leave today, so the network backup rotation covers T-2001 and T-2013, which gives E-303.\n  - E-202 is on leave on 26 March, so the CRM/payroll backup rotation covers T-2002, which gives E-203.\n\nEveryone else is the engineer on call for the owning rotation when the ticket is due.",
